#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Makes samples/ace-rs/pdf, for tools/samples/gather and PLAN.md 4.9: PDFs with what ace3's PDFAnalyzer
reads, encrypted in each way it reports, and broken in the ways that decide what it and pdf-parser.py
do. The real samples have none of the first and little of the second.

    make-pdf <out dir>

Run it on the pdf-libraries image, which has pikepdf (tools/library-diff/run builds that image):

    docker run --rm -u "$(id -u)" -v "$PWD:/w" -w /w <image> python tools/samples/make-pdf samples/ace-rs/pdf

Most are written by hand, byte by byte, because a library wouldn't write them. The encrypted ones go
through pikepdf, which picks random keys, so those bytes differ each run. The manifest holds their
hashes, and the files are in git. The URLs are example.com's.
"""

